# Profile layer for __PLUGIN_NAME__.
#
# `dsh plugin --profile <p> add -w <path>` promotes this package into
# dsh.profile.bundles; this file is then composed as that bundle's layer.
#
# A row has exactly EIGHT legal keys:
#   id, name, config, group, disabled, inject   (loader EntryOptions)
#   intercept, isolate                          (added by the loader's isolate module)
# Nothing else is legal.
#   id        - stable, short, kebab-case. Later patch layers target THIS.
#   name      - the INSTALLED PACKAGE NAME. Node must be able to resolve it.
#   config    - every key is optional; src/config.ts supplies the defaults.
#   group     - marks this entry as a nested group.
#   disabled  - true removes the row; there is no `remove` directive.
#   inject    - EVERY entry is required and blocking. Never list a cordis core
#               member (logger, events, reflect, registry, fiber, root): they are
#               plain properties, not services, so the plugin silently never loads.
#   intercept - per-entry intercept config (Dict).
#   isolate   - give this entry its own realm for the named services.
#
# Verify with:
#   node $HOME/.dsh/profiles/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh/lib/bin.js --profile web --dump-config
- insert:
    - id: __PLUGIN_ID__
      name: __PLUGIN_NAME__
      config:
        defaultMode: upper
        maxLength: 10000
